      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[3].Bodies.Array.size
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[0].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: This elevator ascends directly and appears to be a hazard. It is a wonder
        no one ever thought to put a fence around it. Especially after the incident.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[1].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: 'The elevator is controlled by cores: Diamond shaped light crystals.
        Remeber that the smaller gems will not work as substitutes here.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[2].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: 'The tower wasn''t always 5 floors tall. In fact Count Ester threw quite
        a fit when her precious elevator was first modified. "An affront against
        the gods" she had said. In honesty, there was probably something wrong with
        her. '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[3].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: 'The elevator was almost shut down after a catastophic incident in 5
        BD. During the rush into the tower, the elevator was activated with people
        half on, half off. The ncident resulted in 5 injured parties and 1 death.
        However, in the aftermath, no one was held accountable, and the casualties
        dismissed as unfortunate accidents. Since then elevator use was controlled
        much more closely, but this did not prevent later tragedies. '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
