      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[0].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 1: Skyfall'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[1].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 2: Skyfall 1'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[2].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 3: Skyfall 2'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[3].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 4: The two dragons'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[4].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 4: Skyfall 3'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[2].Bodies.Array.size
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[3].Bodies.Array.size
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[4].Bodies.Array.size
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[0].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: Not long after CW1, an array of natural disasters began to hit the land.
        These occured in three, advancing stages, of progressing severity. While
        originally the cause was unknown, eventually scientist Olivia Helinadottir
        would prove a link to the use and production of Caelestium.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[1].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: 'The first round of disasters where minor ones, and many did not notice
        the threat at this point. The start of S1 is officially marked by the first
        spontaneous fire in Verte, but many believe it may have started sooner. Areas
        most affected by CW1 saw mass plant death and suspect levels of burns on
        local wildlife. At the time, this was thought to be residual from the warm
        caused by unknown enemy weapons. S1 also saw mass deaths caused by the curse,
        but the link between these was not known at the time. '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[2].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: S2 saw a drastic increase in the number of disasters. S2 was officially
        marked by the disaster of Adjur II. In the years that followed, large scale,
        spontaneous fires became common place, leading to most of the populance moving
        to fireproof materials. Several key medicines appeared to loose efficacy
        entirely, and the curse spread further. S2 also saw effects taking place
        globally, not just in war affected zones as in S1. Although obvious in hindsight,
        at the time, all 3 major nations were focused on the second Caelestium War.
        Therefore nothing much was done until S3.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[3].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: Although not the focus of the major powers, during CW2, the first of
        the two dragons took notice of Skyfall. The Dark Dragon began work on an
        emergency solution to move humanity underground to avoid the calamities wrought
        by Skyfall.  Per Their design, all of the necessary food, water and energy
        would be produced within a closed system, with external power at a minimum.
        After Hesterdottir released their first theory, They also began work on the
        road to recovery.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[4].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: Skyfall 3 is marked by the burning of the last of Verte's great reserve.
        This occured only 2 years after the end of the Last Caelestium War. This
        great fire lit in a wave across the world, and burned for 3 days and nights.
        In the aftermath, anything left outside was burnt to ash. The only remaining
        plants from before the final burn are the ones that were in the shade of
        others, or the ones preserved inside. People and animals that couldn't get
        to shelter in time died similarly, while a large majority of the remining
        surviours suffered burns and breathing issues. Fortunately, many areas that
        had already been incinerated by S1 and S2 were spared, although plant life
        was similarly scarce there. After S3, the number of disasters and instances
        of the curse increased. Faced with the ensuing calamity, the Light Dragon
        sought the Dark, and They led us beneath the ground to wait out the rest
        of the calamities.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4429480717681690033, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Sprite
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bb1b9c10fc0396945a358340ff719672, type: 3}
