    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[0].Subtitle
      value: Chapter 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[1].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 2: The first Caelestium War'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[2].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 3: The second Caelestium War'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[3].Subtitle
      value: 'Chapter 4: The tragedy of Adjur II '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[2].Bodies.Array.size
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: Lore.Array.data[3].Bodies.Array.size
      value: 1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[0].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: In the time before, there was abunance. The discovery of Caelestium
        meant resources were plentiful and life was easy. But 'plenty' was never
        enough. So we sought more.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[1].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: 'The true ''beginning of the end'' was the first Caelestium War. Then
        superpowers, Vehte and Corvalte got into a conflict over a source that fell
        into the Northern sea. Unsurprisingly, any power capable of creating great
        abundance was also capable of great harm. Although the conflict was mostly
        limited to un-inhabited zones, towards the end war began to damage even the
        capital cities of both nations. The deadliest war yet ultimately ended in
        a truce, but also ignited an arms race in the years to follow. This created
        a desperate race to develop more advanced applications of Caelestium. '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[2].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: 'The second Caelestium War was the result of increasing concerns about
        Caelestium production. In the aftermath of the conflict, Vehte and Corvalte
        turned their competition to the younger state of Rosenval. After the first
        war, Rosenval was seen as a critical ally that could have served asw a tie
        breaker.  However, securing this relationship was difficult, as Rosenval
        looked down on conflict, and refused to co-operate with the other nations.
        This all changed when the sky fell. Rosenval, blaming the other two nations
        for their greed, sought to subdue the other nations by force. In the ensuing
        conflict, Corvalte and Rosenval created a treaty forbidding the aggressive
        use of Caelestium. However, Verte took advantage of this limitation to gain
        an edge in military advancement. '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3904203509725669748, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'Lore.Array.data[3].Bodies.Array.data[0]'
      value: The final great war was triggered after the catastophy in Adjur II.
        This saw the destruction of the majority of Corvalte's remaining military
        force, as well as its techincal and scientific sectors. While the true cause
        of the tragedy remains unknown, many of Rosenval's greatest, including their
        late leader Hester, believe it was the fault of Verte's military experiements.
        This lead to Rosenval declaring war, with Verte launching a retalitory invasion
        one year in. Peace was only won 3 years after, when a civilian coup  overthrew
        the old leaders of Verte and subsequently brokered peace.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6924618555201837704, guid: a3d8974cfdc93d8418cedce593de086e, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'RequisiteFlags.Array.data[0]'
      value: b1
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
